1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,944
Hey everyone, welcome to Car Service
Podcast.

2
00:00:03,294 --> 00:00:05,574
I'm Sam, and with me is Alex.

3
00:00:05,924 --> 00:00:09,116
Today we're diving into transfer case
repair at Golden Horse.

4
00:00:09,466 --> 00:00:12,418
Our guest is a French driver who loves his
SUV.

5
00:00:12,767 --> 00:00:15,263
Bonjour, I'm Julien.

6
00:00:15,613 --> 00:00:17,797
Julien, thanks for joining us on the show.

7
00:00:18,147 --> 00:00:21,171
So, what brought you to Golden Horse in
the first place?

8
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:25,745
A weird whine from the rear every time I
accelerated hard.

9
00:00:26,095 --> 00:00:29,575
A whine? That sounds like a classic
transfer case symptom.

10
00:00:29,925 --> 00:00:32,373
Did any warning light pop up on the
dashboard?

11
00:00:32,723 --> 00:00:37,091
No light, just the noise and a faint
vibration through the floor.

12
00:00:37,441 --> 00:00:38,737
How did you book the appointment?

13
00:00:39,086 --> 00:00:43,694
I booked online at golden-horse.ae, it
took two minutes.

14
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:47,236
The website is pretty smooth and shows the
price upfront.

15
00:00:47,586 --> 00:00:49,578
What was the workshop like when you
arrived?

16
00:00:49,928 --> 00:00:55,736
Clean, organized, Al Quoz 3 on 22nd
Street, Warehouse 4.

17
00:00:56,086 --> 00:00:58,894
Warehouse 4 is the main service bay,
right?

18
00:00:59,244 --> 00:01:03,972
Exactly, the team greeted me in French,
which felt personal.

19
00:01:04,322 --> 00:01:06,842
That's a nice personal touch for a foreign
customer.

20
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:10,240
Did they explain the diagnosis clearly
before any work?

21
00:01:10,589 --> 00:01:15,773
Yes, they ran a quick scan, found worn
gears inside the case.

22
00:01:16,123 --> 00:01:19,195
Worn gears inside the transfer case can
cause that whine.

23
00:01:19,545 --> 00:01:24,033
Right, they showed me the wear on a
monitor, very transparent.

24
00:01:24,383 --> 00:01:27,575
Transparent, no hidden surprises or
upsells.

25
00:01:27,925 --> 00:01:29,941
How long did the repair take overall?

26
00:01:30,291 --> 00:01:34,275
A few hours, they kept me updated
throughout the process.

27
00:01:34,625 --> 00:01:36,497
And the price you paid for the repair?

28
00:01:36,847 --> 00:01:42,511
From 350 AED, matched the online quote
exactly.

29
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:47,012
Great, the service page lists price from
350 AED.

30
00:01:47,362 --> 00:01:49,594
How does the SUV feel now on the road?

31
00:01:49,944 --> 00:01:54,480
Smooth, the whine is gone, power delivery
feels solid.

32
00:01:54,830 --> 00:01:57,254
That's exactly what we like to hear from a
happy driver.

33
00:01:57,604 --> 00:02:00,076
Did they give you any maintenance tips for
the future?

34
00:02:00,426 --> 00:02:04,650
They said check the transfer case fluid at
every service interval.

35
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,312
Smart advice, fresh fluid keeps gears
happy and quiet.

36
00:02:08,662 --> 00:02:11,710
Now, Omar joins us for a quick expert tip.

37
00:02:12,059 --> 00:02:14,435
Hi, I'm Omar from Golden Horse.

38
00:02:14,785 --> 00:02:18,097
Omar, which dashboard warning lights
should I never ignore?

39
00:02:18,447 --> 00:02:23,247
From what we see, check engine, oil
pressure, brake, battery, temperature.

40
00:02:23,597 --> 00:02:27,125
Got it, act fast on those lights to avoid
bigger issues.

41
00:02:27,475 --> 00:02:30,091
Thanks, Omar, that's a solid reminder.

42
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:32,241
Anytime, happy to help.

43
00:02:32,591 --> 00:02:34,703
Time for our Service Duel segment.

44
00:02:35,053 --> 00:02:38,365
Fix now vs wait: a faint clunk from the
transfer case.

45
00:02:38,714 --> 00:02:41,810
Fix now — clunks usually mean gear wear
starting.

46
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,920
Wait — sometimes it's just a loose bolt or
mount.

47
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:48,414
But loose bolts can snap under load and
cause damage.

48
00:02:48,764 --> 00:02:51,980
True, but a quick inspection costs little
and gives peace.

49
00:02:52,330 --> 00:02:55,426
Exactly, better safe than stranded on a
highway.

50
00:02:55,776 --> 00:02:58,080
Agreed, fix now wins this duel.

51
00:02:58,430 --> 00:02:59,894
Service Duel settled.

52
00:03:00,244 --> 00:03:03,052
Julien, any final thoughts on the whole
experience?

53
00:03:03,401 --> 00:03:07,697
Honestly, worth every dirham, trust the
crew completely.

54
00:03:08,047 --> 00:03:10,087
Love that honesty and confidence.

55
00:03:10,437 --> 00:03:12,453
Thanks for sharing your story with our
listeners.

56
00:03:12,803 --> 00:03:15,851
Merci, keep the podcast rolling.

57
00:03:16,201 --> 00:03:19,897
If you need transfer case work, book at
golden-horse.ae.

58
00:03:20,247 --> 00:03:24,351
Open 10 to 8, Al Quoz 3, Warehouse 4,
Dubai.

59
00:03:24,701 --> 00:03:27,533
See you next episode on Car Service
Podcast.

60
00:03:27,883 --> 00:03:29,563
Drive safe, everyone.

61
00:03:29,912 --> 00:03:32,864
Did you notice any change in fuel economy
after the fix?

62
00:03:33,214 --> 00:03:37,438
Slight improvement, the engine doesn't
work as hard now.

63
00:03:37,788 --> 00:03:40,644
That's a nice bonus for a transfer case
repair.

64
00:03:40,994 --> 00:03:43,490
Was the team communicative throughout the
whole process?

65
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:48,064
Yes, they called me when parts arrived and
when it was ready.

66
00:03:48,414 --> 00:03:52,062
Communication builds trust, especially for
a first visit.

67
00:03:52,412 --> 00:03:54,524
Did they offer any warranty on the repair?

68
00:03:54,874 --> 00:03:59,722
They mentioned a standard workshop
guarantee, but I didn't ask details.

69
00:04:00,071 --> 00:04:02,327
It's good to know they stand behind their
work.

70
00:04:02,677 --> 00:04:05,365
Would you recommend Golden Horse to other
French expats?

71
00:04:05,715 --> 00:04:09,771
Absolutely, the service felt professional
and personal.

72
00:04:10,121 --> 00:04:12,185
Great to hear a strong endorsement.

73
00:04:12,535 --> 00:04:15,559
Before we wrap, any tip for drivers
hearing a whine?

74
00:04:15,909 --> 00:04:19,653
Don't ignore it, get it checked before it
worsens.

75
00:04:20,003 --> 00:04:22,043
Solid advice from experience.

76
00:04:22,393 --> 00:04:25,273
Omar, any extra tip for transfer case
care?

77
00:04:25,622 --> 00:04:28,862
Check fluid level and condition at every
oil change.

78
00:04:29,212 --> 00:04:31,132
Simple habit, big payoff.

79
00:04:31,482 --> 00:04:33,978
Thanks, Omar, that's a great reminder.

80
00:04:34,328 --> 00:04:35,312
My pleasure.

81
00:04:35,662 --> 00:04:39,430
Back to Service Duel: fix now vs wait for
a leaking seal.

82
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:42,924
Fix now — leaks only get worse and
contaminate fluid.

83
00:04:43,274 --> 00:04:46,562
Wait — a tiny seep might be okay for a
short trip.

84
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:49,312
But contaminated fluid kills gears fast.

85
00:04:49,661 --> 00:04:52,157
True, better to replace the seal early.

86
00:04:52,507 --> 00:04:53,947
Fix now wins again.

87
00:04:54,297 --> 00:04:55,377
Duel settled.

88
00:04:55,727 --> 00:04:58,319
Julien, one last word for our listeners?

89
00:04:58,669 --> 00:05:02,773
Trust your ears, trust the pros, drive
safe.

90
00:05:03,123 --> 00:05:04,299
Perfect closing.

91
00:05:04,649 --> 00:05:07,865
Remember to book at golden-horse.ae for
any drivetrain work.

92
00:05:08,215 --> 00:05:12,319
Open 10 to 8, Al Quoz 3, Warehouse 4,
Dubai.

93
00:05:12,668 --> 00:05:14,756
Thanks for listening to Car Service
Podcast.

94
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:17,746
See you next time, drive safe everyone.
